# Playwright UI Automation Tests

Automated UI test project built with Python, Playwright, and Pytest.

The project covers practice websites and will be expanded gradually with new QA Playground sections.

## Current Coverage

- Expand Testing: login scenarios
- QA Playground: input field scenarios

QA Playground Input Fields coverage includes typing, submitting, placeholder validation, appending text, reading values, clearing fields, disabled inputs, and readonly inputs.

## Tech Stack

- Python
- Playwright
- Pytest
- pytest-html

## Project Approach

- Tests are isolated with a new browser page per test.
- Shared fixtures are stored in `conftest.py`.
- QA Playground tests use the Page Object Model.
- Common page behavior is stored in `BasePage`.
- Page-specific locators and actions are stored in page object classes such as `InputFieldsPage`.
- New practice pages can be added with a dedicated page object and test file.

## Project Structure

```text
Playwright-Python/
├── pages/
│   ├── base_page.py
│   └── input_fields_page.py
├── tests/
│   ├── test_expandtesting_login.py
│   └── test_qaplayground_input_field.py
├── conftest.py
├── pytest.ini
├── reports/
└── Readme
```

## Installation

```bash
pip install pytest playwright pytest-html
playwright install chromium
```

## Run Tests

Run all tests:

```bash
pytest -v
```

Run QA Playground input field tests:

```bash
pytest tests/test_qaplayground_input_field.py -v
```

Run tests with an HTML report:

```bash
pytest tests/test_qaplayground_input_field.py --html=reports/test_qaplayground_input_field.html
```
